.TH CLAUDEME 1 "February 2026" "claudeme 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claudeme \- Claude Code account switcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claudeme
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B claudeme
is a terminal application for managing and switching between multiple Claude Code
accounts (e.g., personal pro and company teams). Each account gets an isolated
\fBCLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\fR with its own authentication, settings, and session state.
A shell hook exports the environment variable so \fBclaude\fR uses the right account.
.SH HOW IT WORKS
Each account is stored in its own directory at
\fB~/.config/claudeme/profiles/<email>/\fR.
When you run \fBclaudeme add\fR, Claude Code is launched with
\fBCLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\fR pointing to a staging directory. After you authenticate and
exit, the directory is renamed to match the account email.
.PP
Switching accounts sets the active profile in \fBprofiles.json\fR. The shell hook
exports \fBCLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\fR to point to the active profile's directory. No
file swapping or keychain manipulation is needed.
.PP
Short aliases can be assigned to accounts (e.g., \fBwork\fR for
\fBuser@company.com\fR) and used with any command that accepts an account
reference.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Account Management
.TP
.B claudeme
Launch interactive TUI to select an account.
.TP
.B claudeme add
Add a new account. Launches \fBclaude\fR for authentication, then registers the
account by email.
.TP
.B claudeme list\fR, \fBclaudeme ls
List all accounts with active marker and aliases.
.TP
.B claudeme set \fIALIAS\fR|\fIEMAIL
Switch to an account.
.TP
.B claudeme as \fIALIAS\fR|\fIEMAIL\fR [\fICLAUDE-ARGS\fR...]
Launch \fBclaude\fR with that account without changing the active one, so two
terminals can run two accounts in parallel.
.TP
.B claudeme pin \fIALIAS\fR|\fIEMAIL\fR, \fBclaudeme unpin
Pin the current shell to one account by setting \fBCLAUDEME_PROFILE\fR. A pinned
shell overrides the active profile and skips auto\-switching. Requires the shell
hook (\fBeval "$(claudeme hook)"\fR).
.TP
.B claudeme current\fR, \fBclaudeme whoami
Show the active account.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-dir
Output only the profile directory path (used by shell hook).
.TP
.B \-\-short
Output alias or email (used by status line).
.RE
.TP
.B claudeme remove \fIALIAS\fR|\fIEMAIL\fR, \fBclaudeme rm
Remove an account and its config directory.
.TP
.B claudeme reset
Remove all accounts, aliases, and config. Start fresh.
.SS Aliases
.TP
.B claudeme alias add \fINAME\fR \fIEMAIL
Create an alias for an account email.
.TP
.B claudeme alias list\fR, \fBclaudeme alias ls
List all aliases.
.TP
.B claudeme alias rm \fINAME
Remove an alias.
.SS Auto-switch
.TP
.B claudeme auto
Check rules for the current directory and output an \fBexport\fR command to
stdout if a match is found (designed for shell hook eval).
.TP
.B claudeme rule add \fIPATTERN\fR \fIALIAS\fR|\fIEMAIL
Add an auto-switch rule mapping a directory pattern to an account.
.TP
.B claudeme rule list\fR, \fBclaudeme rule ls
List all auto-switch rules.
.TP
.B claudeme rule rm \fIPATTERN
Remove an auto-switch rule.
.TP
.B claudeme config auto_apply on\fR|\fBoff
Toggle whether matching rules auto-switch or just warn.
.TP
.B claudeme hook
Print the shell hook for \fB.zshrc\fR or \fB.bashrc\fR.
Add \fBeval "$(claudeme hook)"\fR to your shell rc file.
.TP
.B claudeme help\fR, \fBclaudeme \-\-help\fR, \fBclaudeme \-h
Show help information.
.SS Usage reports
.TP
.B claudeme projects \fR[\fB\-\-cost\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fIQUERY\fR]
List the projects found in the shared transcript directory. Transcript folders
are clustered by working directory, so subdirectories, prototypes and worktree
copies fold into the checkout they belong to.
\fB\-\-cost\fR adds a cost column, which scans every transcript, and prints each
project's spend per day and per skill beneath its row. Both are summed from the
working directories the project owns, so they add up to its cost column.
\fB\-\-all\fR includes transcript folders that hold no sessions.
.TP
.B claudeme usage \fR[\fIQUERY\fR] [\fB\-\-top\fR \fIN\fR]
Report token spend for one project, or for all of them when \fIQUERY\fR is
omitted. An exact project name wins; otherwise \fIQUERY\fR matches any project
whose name or path contains it. Breaks spend down by day, model, skill,
session, main loop vs subagent, and agent type. \fB\-\-top\fR limits the session
table
(default 20).
.TP
.B claudeme archive \fR[\fB\-\-days\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-install\fR] [\fB\-\-uninstall\fR] [\fB\-\-status\fR]
Move transcripts older than \fIN\fR days (default 7) out of the tree Claude Code
manages and into a gzipped mirror at
.IR ~/.config/claudeme/shared/archive .
Claude Code deletes transcripts from its own tree after \fBcleanupPeriodDays\fR;
archived ones are beyond its reach, and \fBprojects\fR and \fBusage\fR read both
trees, so reports get deeper over time rather than truncating at the retention
window. Archived sessions are readable by \fBusage\fR but not resumable by
Claude Code.
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR reports what would move and touches nothing.
\fB\-\-status\fR shows the schedule and the size of each tree.
\fB\-\-install\fR schedules a daily run at 04:00 through launchd (macOS only);
\fB\-\-uninstall\fR removes it, leaving already-archived transcripts in place.
.PP
Costs use public list pricing; on a Max or Pro subscription the real invoice is
zero. Records are deduped by request id, because resuming a session replays
earlier turns into the new transcript. Every report prints the date range it
covers, which is bounded by the transcripts still on disk.
.SH TUI KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Up/Down
Navigate the account list.
.TP
.B Enter
Select the highlighted account.
.TP
.B d\fR, \fBx
Delete the highlighted account (with confirmation).
.TP
.B /
Filter/search accounts.
.TP
.B q\fR, \fBEsc\fR, \fBCtrl+C
Quit without making changes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Set by the shell hook to point to the active profile directory. Claude Code reads
all configuration and credentials from this directory instead of \fB~/.claude/\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/claudeme/profiles.json
Account metadata and active account email.
.TP
.I ~/.config/claudeme/aliases.json
Alias-to-email mappings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/claudeme/rules.json
Auto-switch rules (directory pattern to account mappings).
.TP
.I ~/.config/claudeme/settings.json
User preferences (auto_apply on/off).
.TP
.I ~/.config/claudeme/profiles/<email>/
Isolated CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR for an account (replaces ~/.claude/).
.TP
.I ~/.config/claudeme/profiles/<email>.json
Claude Code main config for an account (replaces ~/.claude.json).
.SH EXAMPLES
Add two accounts:
.RS
.nf
claudeme add          # login with personal, then /exit
claudeme add          # login with work, then /exit
.fi
.RE
.TP
Create aliases:
.RS
.nf
claudeme alias add personal user@gmail.com
claudeme alias add work user@company.com
.fi
.RE
.TP
Switch accounts:
.B claudeme set work
.TP
Auto-switch by directory:
.RS
.nf
claudeme config auto_apply on
claudeme rule add ~/Developer/work work
.fi
.RE
.TP
Install the shell hook:
.B eval "$(claudeme hook)"
